# Project AI harness

Cursor reads `AGENTS.md` at the repo root natively — it is the **single source of truth** and wins over any rule here. Follow it in full, especially:

- **Git & branching (§6):** never commit/push on `master`; work on
  `type/###-kebab-slug` branches (`feat|fix|chore|docs|refactor|test`).
- **Permissions (§7):** always-allowed (read, build commands, edit under `src/`),
  confirmation-required (commits/pushes/merges, `npm install`, memory edits),
  never (`master`, `dist/`, `.astro/`, `node_modules/`, `.qodo/`).
- **Memory & self-learning (§8):** after every task update
  `.harness/memory/lessons.md`, `decisions.md`, `project-state.md` via the
  `memory-update` skill.

## Shared harness locations

| Path | Contents |
|---|---|
| `.harness/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` | Reusable procedures (see AGENTS.md §9 for the index) |
| `.harness/agents/<name>.md` | Sub-agent definitions (full personas) |
| `.harness/memory/` | Cross-agent persistent memory |

Follow the matching `SKILL.md` whenever the task matches its description. Cursor
does not auto-load `.harness/skills` — read the relevant skill file explicitly
when its topic comes up (e.g. resume content → `add-resume-entry`, GIF workflow →
`update-readme-gif`, finishing any change → `verify-build`).